  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper introduces predictive and structural quantum kernels derived from quantum hidden Markov models and evaluates them on a synthetic binary market‑movement dataset of 500 samples. Using SVC and k‑NN classifiers, the quantum kernels achieve up to 0.980 out‑of‑sample accuracy in the predictive task versus 0.916 for classical RBF kernels, and up to 0.949 versus 0.903 in the structural task. A kernel matrix is also demonstrated on IBM’s 72‑qubit Nazca device using projected‑kernel measurements.",
